    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSet at the end of an exclusive, deeply private cul-de-sac off Torquay Road, this attractive, sylvan-type detached family home offers the ultimate sanctuary right close to the heart of Foxrock Village. Having undergone a substantial and extensive refurbishment and extension only 10 years ago this home offers a modern, future proofed home full of character. Standing proudly on a generous plot of almost a third of an acre, the property is safely enveloped behind remote-controlled electronic gates. This ensures immense privacy and a genuinely secluded atmosphere, yet leaves you merely moments from the very best of Ireland's infrastructure. Commuters and busy families will enjoy unparalleled convenience with the Luas, M50, N11, and the Quality Bus Corridor (QBC) all right on your doorstep. Furthermore, major employers within the Sandyford Business District—such as Microsoft and The Beacon Hospital—are well within striking distance, seamlessly balancing an idyllic, quiet retreat with effortless connectivity..\n\nFor families with children, this superb infrastructural network provides a direct gateway to Dublin's finest primary, secondary, and third-level educational institutions. Closer to home, a premium education is available just moments away, with elite schools like Loreto College Foxrock and Nord Anglia International School Dublin sitting practically in the neighborhood.\n\nStep inside this C2 BER-rated residence to discover an impressively spacious and brilliantly well-appointed interior where large rooms and light-filled areas govern the layout. The journey begins in a large, inviting entrance hall, beautifully framed by a glazed landing overlooking the space from above. Double doors lead from the hall into a gracious drawing room boasting dramatic, double-height ceilings that are also overlooked by the upper gallery. Ideal for grand entertaining, bi-folding doors open from the drawing room into a formal dining room, which seamlessly connects to a cozy family room. This flows effortlessly into the bright kitchen and breakfast room, complete with a practical utility room and a guest cloakroom. Designed for modern living, the ground floor also features a dedicated home office to the front, a second en-suite bedroom, and a sprawling principal bedroom suite featuring its own large en-suite bathroom. Upstairs, the expansive, airy landing leads to two additional double bedrooms, both of which also enjoy private en-suite facilities.\n\nThe exterior of the property is equally impressive and tailored for relaxation. Outside, extensive manicured lawns, thoughtfully planted borders, and paved patios are wrapped in mature greenery, creating many hidden, private suntraps to enjoy throughout the day. The grounds are completed by a substantial double detached garage and a separate storeroom, providing excellent additional security and storage."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nHall - \nGracious reception hall with balcony above. Accommodation off and stairs to level above. Tiled floors.\n\nDrawing Room - 5.7m x 5.5m\nLarge rear facing living room with vaulted ceilings, timber floors, a feature fireplace and TV point.\n\nFamily Room - 6.2m x 3.3m\nEveryday reception room with TV point and open plan with large dining room.\n\nDining Room - 5.2m x 4.2m\nBi-fold doors leading from the dining room. Wall-to-wall glass and French doors leading to the gardens.\n\nOffice - 3.1m x 3.6m\nFront facing reception room with fireplace and timber floors.\n\nKitchen / Breakfastroom - 3.1m x 4.7m\nTriple aspect room comprising a floor and eye level units, a central island, Aga, timber floors, granite work surfaces, electric oven, gas hob and coving to ceiling. Sliding doors leading to the rear garden.\n\nUtility Room - 3m x 2.3m\nFloor and eye level fitted units. Provisions for a washing machine and dishwasher. Sink.\n\nGuest Cloakroom - \nWith toilet and wash hand basin.\n\nBedroom 1 - 6m x 5.8m\nPrincipal bedroom of large proportions with fitted wardrobes, a door leading to the gardens and ensuite bathroom off.\n\nEnsuite Bathroom - 3.8m x 2\nStand alone bath, separate shower, toilet and wash hand basin.\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.7m x 2.7m\nFront facing bedroom with ensuite off.\n\nEnsuite - \nShower, toilet and wash hand basin.\n\nLanding - \nLanding with balcony overlooking the reception hall to the front and the Drawing room to the rear.\n\nBedroom 3 - 5.7m x 4.5m\nBeautiful, large double bedroom which is light filled and has timber floors. Ensuite off.\n\nEnsuite Bathroom - 3.2m x 2.6m\nBath, separate shower, wc & whb. Part tiled.\n\nBedroom 4 - 4m x 3.75m\nLarge bedroom with vaulted ceiling, triple aspect and fitted wardrobes.\n\nEnsuite - 2.3m x 2.3m\nShower, wc & whb.\n\nGarage - \nSubstantial detached garage with pitched roof over together with a Plant Room behind.\n\nGardens - \nThe property is set near the end of a small cul de sac and behind electronic controlled gates onto a pebbled forecourt surrounded by lawns, patio areas together with a fine selection of mature plants, trees and shrubs. The overall plot is approximately c. 0.3ac.\n\n"
      },
